=== PE 908: Clock Sequence Theory ===

A clock sequence with period P has elements a[0..P-1].
The n-th segment sums to n, so the cumulative sums
of the repeating sequence must hit all triangular numbers.

Let Σ = sum(a[0..P-1]) be the period sum.
Then the cumulative sum at position m*P + r is:
  S(m*P + r) = m*Σ + prefix(r)

For this to hit T_k = k(k+1)/2, we need:
  T_k ≡ prefix(r) (mod Σ) for some r
  and also T_k ≥ prefix(r) with the right quotient.

=== Known values ===
C(3)  = 3
C(4)  = 7
C(10) = 561

The problem reduces to counting sequences where all
triangular numbers are "covered" by the period pattern.
